    "title": "Rotting Oranges",
    "category": "Queue",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "problemStatement": "You are given an m \u00d7 n grid where: 0 represents an empty cell. 1 represents a fresh orange. 2 represents a rotten orange. Every minute, any fresh orange adjacent (up, down, left, or right) to a rotten orange also becomes rotten. Return the minimum number of minutes required until no fresh oranges remain. If it is impossible, return -1.",
    "input": "Integers m and n An m \u00d7 n integer grid",
    "output": "A single integer representing the required minutes.",
    "constraints": "1 <= m, n <= 100"
